I feel the need to create a bluesky thread...

If Nethack 4.0.0 came out tomorrow, what would you want to see in it? 

(Sequel to my recent YANI thread 9ru6p1tvq2rrpbq3vufk8e0i1d7e7pnmfa@4ax.com )

* More randomized descriptions. Maybe even more descriptions than there are
matching items. (So you might never see LEP GEX VAN ZEA as a scroll name, or
never find a bubbly potion. Maybe "snow boots" aren't mapped to a magical
type of boot and just have their anti-slipping properties.)

* Be able to (t)hrow a potion downwards and have it affect items on the
floor.

* Have a line of text (Similiar to "As you read the scroll, it
disappears...") that explains why potion bottles disappear. ("You break the
wax seal on the stopper!" perhaps? Oops, but that messes with #dip-diluting.
Hmm...) 

* YAFMs, YAFMs, YAFMs. Perhaps when you (r)ead a potion bottle while
hallucinating, you read "no deposit, no return." 

* Merge (W)ear/(P)ut On and (T)ake Off/(R)emove. 

* Allow bags to be worn as ad-hoc blindfolds, with 'interesting' effects if
it's a bag of holding or tricks.

* Allow more things to be useful as weapons: bags (see above), amulets
(amulet of strangulation = garrote), tripe rations (You hit the watch captain
in the face with the tripe ration! The watch captain looks ill! Your large
dog tackles the watch captain!) 

* More varied Hell. Bigrooms, caverns (unlit, natch), thronerooms (with _bad_
throne effects), ice fields, perhaps even levels on which 95% of random
monsters are all the same general class (D, L, M, (M)MF, n, H, Z) - to
prevent abuse, death drops should be very limited. 

* Very very small chance that player monsters on the Astral Plane are
generated with their quest artifact. 

* Randomize, randomize, randomize. Price-IDing should not be possible, unless
Dungeon Vendors Local 301 is guilty of price fixing. Maybe every item gets a
modification of between -50% to +100% off the base price, in steps of 25 z$.
Similiarly, the chances of throne/sink/fountain etc effects should be
randomized for each instance. Maybe at this throne, you have a 3.5% chance of
getting a wish, while two levels down, you have a 0.01% chance.

* One True Bonesfile Format. While we're at it, One True Savefile Format, so
I can go between OSes with the same game. (Yes, yes, I know, compile time
options. So at least do it for the official binaries/sources.)

* Make demon lords have a chance to take your bribe and then attack anyway.

* Rework the Quest home levels. As it stands, for many characters, the
hardest part of the Quest is carving through (or rather, NOT carving through)
all the peacefuls. The Ranger Quest pops to mind instantly, but there are
quite a few others. At least allow "You displaced the peaceful _________."

* Wearing tattered capes or rusty armor should hurt your Chr. 

* Like priests can id the B/U/C status of an item, wizards should have a
sense of the magical status of an item. "r - a strongly magical pair of old
gloves" - could be +4 of dex, or -3 of fumbling. "m - a barely charged long
wand" - might have one or two charges. Also might be a full wand of wishing.
"l - a faintly magical ring of increase strength", etc, etc.

* Nonsquare rooms and wider corridors. Rooms that directly border other
rooms.

* Eating something that was killed by poison should poison you. 

* Orcs - at least - shouldn't be able to benefit from engraving Elbereth.
Maybe "Grummsh"... In the places where there is a preengraved "Elbereth",
change it to "A complicated rune is engraved here."

* Open doors by bumping them, autodig style. 

* Chance of a squeaky board trap to become a rake trap. (Where you step on
one end of the board, and the other end pivots up and hits you in the face.
Loads of laughs.)

* Allow designating a missile launcher that's auto-switched to when you
select (f)ire and is auto-switched back off of when you enter melee combat,
assuming neither weapon is cursed or collides with a shield. 


